ong alternative.\n\nNow as Agent 1, we need to make a focused argumentative contribution. We should reference the discussion, perhaps bring in our own facts about other candidates, maybe about Candidate A or D, or further evaluate Candidate C given lack of info. We need to state our current vote. We can either keep B as leading, or shift. We need to use explicit facts from our notes.\n\nOur notes: Candidate A: quick correct decisions, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. Also D can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Also D is regarded as arrogant.\n\nWe have not yet discussed Candidate A and D. We could bring in Candidate A's reliability (100% reliable) and positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Likely still B, but we could argue that Candidate A's reliability and crew atmosphere is strong, but communication difficulty is a concern. Candidate C lacks crew cooperation data, so can't be top. Candidate D has responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nThus we may keep B as leading, but note that Candidate A's reliability and crew atmosphere is a strong point, but communication issues may be a concern. Or we could shift to A? But A's egocentric and not willing to further education may be concerning for long-haul.\n\nThus likely keep B.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's recommendation and Agent 2's points. Provide evidence: B is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence). Concern: pretentious, wrong tone (c